# __NAME__ React Studio module

Generated sample for Elsa React Studio Preview. The forecast is local demonstration
state; it does not contact a weather service. Replace Acme/example names, behavior,
metadata and license with your module's own choices.

From Module/Client, run `pnpm install` and `pnpm build`. Commit the generated lockfile
and use `pnpm install --frozen-lockfile` for subsequent builds. Then run
`dotnet pack Module/Module.csproj -o artifacts/packages`. Both Module and Host use
NuGet package references only. Until the Preview packages are published, use the
Elsa repository's authoring verification command with its local packed feed.

Make the module package and Elsa packages available in your NuGet sources, then
`dotnet run --project Host --urls http://127.0.0.1:5204` and open `/studio-preview/`.
The sample host uses anonymous development authentication. Configure authentication
and the API origin before using it against a protected server.

`__MODULE_ID__` must be enabled in browser features as well as the server feature.
JS imports React/public Studio packages from the host; private dependencies may be
bundled. Scope CSS to `.__MODULE_ID__` and shared theme tokens. Bump the NuGet module
version whenever shipped JS/CSS changes, because its asset URLs are immutable.
Host API and SDK API major versions are both 1 for this Preview. Contributions use
module-local IDs and explicit ordering; use `api.onDispose` for external resources.
